[aspect-panel] target=Story US-2 (per-cycle LUAR authorship promotion gate: a candidate adapter is promoted only if its twin score is not a CI-distinguishable regression and clears the floor; three-way PASS/BLOCK/HOLD using the candidate's twin_seth_vs_adapter.ci95, HOLD exit 3, INCONCLUSIVE exit 2 on missing/malformed CI, --min-gain default 0.05) of sprint sprint-better-than-human-2026-09-05. Review: `git -C /Users/sethford/Projects/h-uman/.claude/worktrees/sbth-us2 diff sprint-better-than-human-2026-09-05..sbth-us2` (commits 74b95e440 + 7acb4d470). Files: scripts/blind_ab/authorship_promotion_gate.py (decide_promotion, _as_finite_ci95, CLI), scripts/m3_promote.py cmd_promote() hook (exit 5 on any non-PASS; --skip-authorship-gate records OVERRIDDEN), scripts/register_v6_adapter.py annotation, scripts/blind_ab/score_candidate_offline.py call site, one log line in scripts/nightly-retrain.sh, tests scripts/blind_ab/test_authorship_promotion_gate.py (31), scripts/test_m3_promote.py, scripts/test_register_v6_adapter.py, designs/US-2.md §10. Contract: stories.md US-2 + designs/US-2.md in that worktree. Prior gates: verifier PASS x2, critic r2 MERGE. Rules for panelists: read-only; ABSOLUTE paths; run pytest on the three test files plus `python3 .../scripts/test_m3_promote.py`; synthetic JSON under $TMPDIR only; never touch ports 8741/8743; never read ~/.human/adapters registry, ~/.human/blind_ab_human/, memory.db or chat.db; no adapter names beyond those in the diff, no message text/phones/names in output. Judge: correctness (verdict table vs contract; HOLD never folded into PASS anywhere; m3_promote refuses on HOLD/INCONCLUSIVE); edge cases (NaN/inf/inverted/length!=2 CI; serving score missing; candidate exactly at floor; min_gain boundary); security/privacy (paths only, no secrets); regressions (every existing caller of decide_promotion passes the new required arg; nightly-retrain.sh still parses; m3_promote non-gate commands unchanged); maintainability (is 0.05 justified against the measured CI half-width ~0.1 in the design). aspects=['correctness', 'edge-case', 'security', 'regression', 'style']
